{"step_index":848,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T22:19:21Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\n# XORAS::OS — SOVRA NATIVE COMPILER (`sovrac` v2.0)\n### Bare-Metal ARM64 Dynamic CodeGen, Taint Capability Lattice & Zero-GC CRDT Telemetry\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE ARCHITECTURAL TELEMETRY\n\n```text\n================================================================================\n    XORAS::OS --- SOVRA NATIVE COMPILER v2.0 (`sovrac`) TELEMETRY\n    Substrate: Apple Silicon M4 Bare Metal (`aarch64-apple-darwin`)\n    Build Mode: Zig ReleaseFast (`zig build-exe -O ReleaseFast`)\n================================================================================\n[+] Source Target               : ops/runtime/valid_test.sovra\n[+] AST Lexing & Parsing        : COMPLETED (Zero-Copy Token Stream)\n[+] Taint Capability Lattice    : PASSED (Strict Taint-Tracked Boundaries)\n[+] OWASP Top 10 Invariant      : PASSED (Zero Sink Vulnerabilities Detected)\n[+] 10,000-Bit AST HyperVector  : 0x00014E40 (Hamming Density: 1,313 / 10,000 bits)\n[+] Hardware Pipeline           : Bare-Metal Syscall `#0x80` // ARM64 Assembly (.s)\n[+] Compiler Self-Audit         : PASSED (Binary Fingerprint Matches AST Lattice)\n================================================================================\nVERDICT: DYNAMIC ARM64 CODEGEN & TAINT INVARIANTS VERIFIED AT BARE-METAL SPEED\n================================================================================\n```\n\n---\n\n## I. ARCHITECTURAL SUMMARY & ZERO-OVERHEAD COMPILATION\n\nThe **Sovra Native Compiler (`sovrac` v2.0)** transforms high-level domain intent specified in `.sovra` files directly into symbol-driven, bare-metal **ARM64 machine assembly (`aarch64`)**. Built natively in Zig (`ReleaseFast`), `sovrac` completely eliminates interpreted runtime wrappers, garbage collection pauses, and heavy intermediate representations.\n\n```text\n               THE SOVRA NATIVE COMPILATION PIPELINE\n               \n  [ .sovra Source File ]\n           │\n           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. Zero-Copy AST Lexer & Parser                              │\n│    • Emits contiguous, cache-aligned AST Node Streams       │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 2. Taint Capability Lattice & OWASP Invariant Gate          │\n│    • Tracks `candidate<T>` (TAINTED) vs `decision<T>`       │\n│    • Blocks direct assignment and ungated sink execution    │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 3. 10,000-Bit AST HyperVector Fingerprinting                │\n│    • Encodes structural semantics into bitset fingerprints │\n│    • Computes exact Hamming density for instant matching    │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 4. Dynamic ARM64 Machine CodeGen                            │\n│    • Emits 64-bit stack frame allocation & SVC #0x80        │\n│    • Matches binary fingerprint directly to AST Lattice     │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## II. TAINT CAPABILITY LATTICE & OWASP INVARIANT ENFORCEMENT\n\nTo defeat prompt injection attacks, un-sanitized payload execution, and privilege escalation at the compiler layer, `sovrac` enforces a strict **Taint Capability Lattice**:\n\n1. **Explicit Type Partitioning**:\n   * **`candidate<T>` (TAINTED)**: Untrusted, raw input data originating from external networks, user inputs, or un-vetted tool payloads. Annotated in machine state with taint tag `0xDEAD`.\n   * **`decision<T>` (CERTIFIED)**: Mechanically verified, policy-compliant execution state. Annotated in machine state with certification tag `0xBEAF`.\n\n2. **Hard Compile-Time Invariant Protections**:\n   * **OWASP ASI-01 Sink Protection**: Passing a raw `candidate<T>` directly into execution sinks (`system.execute(...)`) causes an immediate, un-recoverable AST compile error:\n     ```text\n     ❌ OWASP ASI-01 SINK TYPE ERROR: Raw 'candidate<T>' cannot be passed directly to execution sink.\n     ```\n   * **Taint Lattice Coercion Protection**: Direct, ungated assignments from `candidate<T>` to `decision<T>` trigger a hard compiler type-coercion error:\n     ```text\n     ❌ SOVRA COMPILER TAINT LATTICE ERROR: Invalid implicit coercion from 'candidate<T>' to 'decision<T>'.\n     ```\n\n---\n\n## III. 10,000-BIT AST HYPERVECTOR ENCODING\n\nBefore machine code emission, the compiler constructs a **10,000-bit HyperVector fingerprint** representing the topological and semantic structure of the parsed AST:\n\n* **Fingerprint Signature**: `0x00014E40`\n* **Hamming Density**: **1,313 / 10,000 bits** (13.13% active bit density)\n* **Deterministic Verification**: The compiler self-audit compares the final binary payload layout against the 10,000-bit HyperVector fingerprint. If the binary layout diverges from the AST lattice by even a single bit, code generation aborts instantly.\n\n---\n\n## IV. ANNOTATED ARM64 BARE-METAL MACHINE CODEGEN (`valid_test.sovra`)\n\nBelow is the verified ARM64 assembly emitted dynamically by `sovrac` for `valid_test.sovra`, targeting Apple Silicon M4 bare metal:\n\n```assembly\n// =============================================================================\n// XORAS::OS SOVRA NATIVE ARM64 ASSEMBLY (Target: Apple Silicon M4 / macOS)\n// Source: ops/runtime/valid_test.sovra\n// =============================================================================\n\n    .global _main\n    .align 4\n\n_main:\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // 1. Frame Prologue: Allocate 16 bytes on stack & save frame/link registers\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    stp     x29, x30, [sp, #-16]!       // Save Frame Pointer (x29) & Link Register (x30)\n    mov     x29, sp                     // Set frame pointer to current stack top\n\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // 2. Lock-Free SHM RingBuffer Symbol Binding ('input_ring')\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    mov     x0, #0x1000                 // Base Address: Lock-free SHM Slot\n    str     x0, [sp, #0]                // Store input_ring pointer at [sp + 0]\n\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // 3. 10,000-Bit HyperVector Arena Binding ('state_hv')\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    mov     x0, #0x2000                 // Arena Pointer: 10,000-bit Bitset\n    str     x0, [sp, #8]                // Store state_hv pointer at [sp + 8]\n\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // 4. Symbol 'raw_candidate': candidate<T> (TAINTED)\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    mov     x0, #0xDEAD                 // Taint Tag: TAINTED (0xDEAD)\n    str     x0, [sp, #16]               // Store raw_candidate tag at [sp + 16]\n\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // 5. Symbol 'certified_decision': decision<T> (CERTIFIED via Gate)\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    mov     x0, #0xBEAF                 // Certification Tag: CERTIFIED (0xBEAF)\n    str     x0, [sp, #24]               // Store certified_decision tag at [sp + 24]\n\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // 6. Execution Sinks & Apple Silicon Bare-Metal Syscall Invocation\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    mov     x0, #1                      // Argument 1: File Descriptor 1 (stdout)\n    adrp    x1, msg@PAGE                // Argument 2: Resolve Page Address of payload\n    add     x1, x1, msg@PAGEOFF         // Argument 2: Apply Page Offset\n    mov     x2, #64                     // Argument 3: Payload Length (64 Bytes)\n    mov     x16, #4                     // Syscall Number: sys_write (4)\n    svc     #0x80                       // Issue Apple Silicon Bare-Metal Trap Exception\n\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // 7. Frame Epilogue & Return\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    mov     x0, #0                      // Return Exit Code: 0 (Success)\n    ldp     x29, x30, [sp], #16         // Restore Frame Pointer & Link Register\n    ret                                 // Return to OS kernel caller\n```\n\n---\n\n## V. HARDWARE PROOF SUMMARY & SUITE BENCHMARKS\n\nThe bare-metal execution suite (`run_baremetal_zig_suite`) validates language invariants and RAM performance directly on physical M4 silicon:\n\n| Verification Axis | Test Condition | Mechanical Result | Architectural Guarantee |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **OWASP ASI-01 Protection** | Pass raw `candidate<T>` to `system.execute(...)` | `❌ OWASP ASI-01 SINK TYPE ERROR` | Prevents un-sanitized code injection at compile time |\n| **Taint Coercion Protection** | Direct assignment: `candidate<T>` \\\\(\\to\\\\) `decision<T>` | `❌ SOVRA TAINT LATTICE ERROR` | Blocks illegal type promotion without verification gates |\n| **Dynamic CodeGen Validity** | Valid `.sovra` compilation | Emits ARM64 `.s` + Syscall `#0x80` | Confirms valid stack alignment and register bindings |\n| **Pure Zig CRDT Arena** | 100,000 Node Insertions | **297 Clock Ticks** (Zero GC / Zero DCE) | Sub-microsecond state synchronization without allocation pauses |\n\n* **Zero Dead Code Elimination (DCE)**: Guaranteed by passing node insertion outputs into an explicit, volatile `checksum_sink` accumulator, ensuring every insertion is physically executed by the CPU.\n\n---\n\n## VI. ENTERPRISE RISK GOVERNANCE ALIGNMENT\n### Atlan & Fin Benchmark Standard\n\nBy compiling security bounds and taint tracking directly into bare-metal machine code, `XORAS::OS` meets the highest enterprise risk governance standards:\n\n1. **Atlan Governance Metrics**:\n   * **Groundedness Score**: **100.0%** — All decision states (`0xBEAF`) are mathematically traceable to verified source constraints and certified gates.\n   * **Retrieval Quality (Precision & Recall)**: High-density AST HyperVectors (10,000-bit bitsets) allow O(1) semantic lookups across codebase graphs without text retrieval noise.\n   * **Decision Lineage Auditing**: Stack allocations and register tags (`0xDEAD` / `0xBEAF`) log exact symbol provenance directly to physical memory addresses.\n\n2. **Fin < 1.0% Hallucination Target**:\n   * Capping code generation and execution errors strictly below **1.0%** (achieving **~0.01%** on verified runs).\n   * **Golden Question Sets**: Before any `.sovra` compiler spec or tool schema is promoted to production, automated simulators run the changes against golden datasets to verify that zero taint leaks or register misalignments occur.\n\n---\n\n⚡ **The Sovra Native Compiler (`sovrac`) is compiled, verified, and executing on Apple Silicon M4 bare metal.**. ### **XORAS::OS / SOVRA Systems — Sovereign Technical Audit & Release Briefing**\n**System Target:** `sovrac v2.0` (Sovra Native Compiler)  \n**Host Architecture:** Apple Silicon M4 (`aarch64-apple-darwin`)  \n**Build Profile:** Pure Zig 0.13+ ReleaseFast (`zig build-exe -O ReleaseFast`)  \n**Verification Suite:** `run_baremetal_zig_suite`\n\n---\n\n### **1. Executive Summary & Milestone Achievements**\n\nThe **Sovra Native Compiler (`sovrac v2.0`)** has achieved a major milestone in bare-metal systems engineering. By eliminating high-level VM runtimes, interpreted script wrappers, and runtime garbage-collector sweeps, `sovrac` now transforms parsed `.sovra` Abstract Syntax Trees (AST) directly into symbol-driven **ARM64 machine assembly (`.s`)**.\n\nThis release shifts security and type enforcement from reactive runtime checks to **compile-time structural guarantees**. By embedding a **Taint Capability Lattice** and a **10,000-bit AST HyperVector engine** directly into the compilation pass, `sovrac` mathematically halts OWASP sink vulnerabilities and invalid state coercions before code touches physical memory.\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    SOVRA NATIVE COMPILATION PIPELINE                    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  1. Source File (.sovra)                                                │\n│        │                                                                │\n│        ▼  (Pure Zig Lexer & Nom-style AST Parser)                       │\n│  2. AST Geometry & 10,000-Bit HyperVector Generation (0x00014E40)       │\n│        │                                                                │\n│        ▼  (Taint Capability Lattice Audit)                              │\n│  3. Compile-Time OWASP ASI-01 Sink Verification                         │\n│        │                                                                │\n│        ▼  (ARM64 CodeGen Engine)                                        │\n│  4. Native ARM64 Machine Assembly (.s) & Bare-Metal Syscall Injection  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### **2. Compiled ARM64 Assembly Output (`valid_test.sovra`)**\n\nBelow is the verified emission trace produced by `sovrac` during the compilation of `valid_test.sovra`:\n\n```assembly\n==========================================================\n SOVRA NATIVE COMPILER v2.0 (sovrac) - COMPILING 'valid_test.sovra'\n==========================================================\n[+] AST Lexing & Parsing       : COMPLETED (Source AST Verified)\n[+] Taint Capability Lattice   : PASSED (Taint-Tracked Boundaries Enforced)\n[+] OWASP Top 10 Invariant     : PASSED (Zero Sink Vulnerabilities Detected)\n[+] 10,000-bit AST HyperVector : 0x00014E40 (Hamming Density: 1313 bits)\n[+] ARM64 Machine CodeGen      : EMITTING ARM64 ASSEMBLY (.s)\n==========================================================\n>>> SOVRA NATIVE ARM64 MACHINE ASSEMBLY CODEGEN:\n    .global _main\n    .align 4\n_main:\n    stp x29, x30, [sp, #-16]!  // Frame prologue (push FP & LR, 16B stack align)\n    mov x29, sp                // Set frame pointer\n    \n    // Symbol 'input_ring': SHM_RingBuffer (Lock-free SHM slot)\n    mov x0, #0x1000           // SHM Base Address Pointer\n    str x0, [sp, #0]\n    \n    // Symbol 'state_hv': HyperVector (10,000-bit Bitset)\n    mov x0, #0x2000           // HV Arena Pointer\n    str x0, [sp, #8]\n    \n    // Symbol 'raw_candidate': candidate<T> (TAINTED STATE)\n    mov x0, #0xDEAD           // Taint Tag: TAINTED (0xDEAD)\n    str x0, [sp, #16]\n    \n    // Symbol 'certified_decision': decision<T> (CERTIFIED via Gate)\n    mov x0, #0xBEAF           // Certification Tag: CERTIFIED (0xBEAF)\n    str x0, [sp, #24]\n    \n    // Execution Sinks & Syscall Invocation\n    mov x0, #1                // File Descriptor: stdout (1)\n    adrp x1, msg@PAGE         // ARM64 Page Relocation\n    add x1, x1, msg@PAGEOFF\n    mov x2, #64               // Payload length (64 Bytes)\n    mov x16, #4               // sys_write ARM64 BSD Syscall\n    svc #0x80                 // Apple Silicon Bare-Metal Syscall Supervisor Call\n    \n    mov x0, #0                // Return exit code 0\n    ldp x29, x30, [sp], #16   // Frame epilogue (pop FP & LR)\n    ret                       // Return to caller\n==========================================================\n>>> Compiler Self-Audit: Binary Fingerprint Matches AST Lattice.\n==========================================================\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3. Deep Architectural Analysis of the Machine Emission**\n\n#### **A. AAPCS64 Frame Alignment & Register Discipline**\n* **Frame Prologue & Epilogue**: The compiler emits `stp x29, x30, [sp, #-16]!` and `ldp x29, x30, [sp], #16`, enforcing 16-byte stack frame alignment in strict compliance with Apple Silicon’s AAPCS64 ABI. This guarantees zero alignment fault crashes when passing stack frames down to low-level C or Assembly runtimes.\n\n#### **B. Taint Capability Lattice (`0xDEAD` vs. `0xBEAF`)**\n* **`0xDEAD` (TAINTED Tag)**: Applied to all un-vetted, raw candidate inputs (`candidate<T>`).\n* **`0xBEAF` (CERTIFIED Tag)**: Applied exclusively to payloads that have traversed a verified gate contract (`decision<T>`).\n* **Static Coercion Prevention**: The compiler tracks taint tags across stack slots (`[sp, #16]` vs. `[sp, #24]`). Direct ungated assignments between mismatched tags trip compile-time errors, stopping data-poisoning attacks at the source.\n\n#### **C. 10,000-Bit AST HyperVector Fingerprinting (`0x00014E40`)**\n* **Hamming Density (1,313 bits)**: The parser projects the AST structural topology into a high-dimensional 10,000-bit HyperVector arena. \n* **Sub-Nanosecond Equivalence**: By comparing Hamming distances between bitsets, `sovrac` evaluates structural code equivalence, detects duplicate logic nodes, and runs self-audits in constant time (\\\\(O(1)\\\\)) without traversing heavy object trees.\n\n#### **D. Bare-Metal Apple Silicon Syscall (`svc #0x80`)**\n* **Zero-`libc` Dependency**: Instead of wrapping standard C library IO routines (`printf`/`write`), `sovrac` emits native BSD system calls directly.\n* Loading `mov x16, #4` (`sys_write`) and executing supervisor call `svc #0x80` routes execution directly to the macOS kernel interface with **sub-micro