{"step_index":851,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-28T22:19:33Z","thinking":"**Initiating Specification Draft**\n\nI've initiated the background process for agent speech. My immediate focus is now on drafting the XORAS/SOVRA DSL Syntax Specification document. I'm starting to generate it at `docs/SOVRA_DSL_SYNTAX_SPECIFICATION.md` within the canonical root.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# XORAS/SOVRA Domain-Specific Language (DSL) v2.0 Syntax Specification\n**Canonical Document ID:** `SOVRA-SPEC-2026-v2.0`  \n**Target Engine:** Sovra Native Compiler (`sovrac` v2.0)  \n**Host Architecture:** Bare-Metal Apple Silicon ARM64 (`aarch64-apple-darwin`)  \n**Security Standard:** OWASP ASI-01 Strict Taint Lattice & Zero-GC Memory Boundaries\n\n---\n\n## 1. Syntax Overview & Type System\n\nThe `.sovra` language is a static, zero-overhead domain-specific language designed for high-concurrency multi-agent orchestration, lock-free shared memory state graphs, and compile-time taint tracking.\n\n### 1.1 Primitive & Security-Bounded Types\n\n| Type Identifier | Description | Compiler Memory Tag | AST Lattice Rules |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `candidate<T>` | Raw, untrusted input payload from network, STT, or external tools. | `0xDEAD` (TAINTED) | Cannot be passed to execution sinks. Cannot implicitly coerce to `decision<T>`. |\n| `decision<T>` | Certified, policy-validated data structure. | `0xBEAF` (CERTIFIED) | Eligible for system sinks (`system.execute`, file I/O, IPC). Must originate from a `gate(...)` sanitizer block. |\n| `SHM_RingBuffer` | Multi-agent lock-free ring buffer slot pointer. | `0x1000` (Base) | Constrained stack allocation `[sp, #0]`. |\n| `HyperVector` | 10,000-bit topological bitset arena reference. | `0x2000` (Arena) | Constrained stack allocation `[sp, #8]`. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Formal Grammar & Code Structure\n\n```ebnf\nProgram         ::= Statement* ;\nStatement       ::= MemoryBinding | Declaration | GateBlock | SinkInvocation | ControlFlow ;\n\nMemoryBinding   ::= \"bind\" Identifier \":\" (\"SHM_RingBuffer\" | \"HyperVector\") \"at\" Address ;\nDeclaration     ::= (\"candidate\" | \"decision\") \"<\" Type \">\" Identifier \"=\" Expression \";\" ;\nGateBlock       ::= \"gate\" \"(\" Identifier \")\" \"{\" ValidationBody \"}\" \"->\" \"decision\" \"<\" Type \">\" Identifier \";\" ;\nSinkInvocation  ::= \"system.execute\" \"(\" \"decision\" \"<\" Type \">\" \")\" \";\" ;\nControlFlow     ::= \"while\" \"(\" Condition \")\" \"{\" Statement* \"}\" ;\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Compiler Invariants & Safety Enforcement\n\n### 3.1 Invariant I: OWASP ASI-01 Sink Guard\nAny attempt to pass a `candidate<T>` directly into an execution sink generates a hard AST compilation error:\n\n```text\n❌ [OWASP ASI-01 SINK TYPE ERROR] Line X: Critical Security Sink Violation!\n   Dangerous execution sink 'system.execute' received raw TAINTED variable 'candidate_var'.\n   REASON: OWASP ASI-01 prevents untainted execution. Must pass through certified 'gate(...)'.\n```\n\n### 3.2 Invariant II: Taint Coercion Prevention\nDirect assignment from `candidate<T>` to `decision<T>` without an explicit `gate` sanitizer block is strictly prohibited:\n\n```text\n❌ [SOVRA COMPILER TAINT LATTICE ERROR] Line X: Taint Coercion Violation!\n   Cannot assign TAINTED 'candidate<T>' variable 'raw_candidate' to CERTIFIED 'decision<T>' variable 'illegal_decision'.\n   REASON: Missing required certified 'gate(...)' block sanitizer!\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Valid `.sovra` Reference Source Example\n\n```sovra\n// =============================================================================\n// XORAS SOVRA REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION: GATED AGENT DATAFLOW\n// =============================================================================\n\nbind input_ring : SHM_RingBuffer at 0x1000;\nbind state_hv   : HyperVector at 0x2000;\n\ncandidate<string> raw_candidate = \"EXTERNAL_INPUT_PAYLOAD\";\n\ng